  // ---------------------------------------------------------- tutorial
  'tut.step': 'Step {n} of {total}',
  'tut.proximo': 'Next',
  'tut.voltar': 'Back',
  'tut.finalizar': 'Got it!',
  'tut.pular': 'Skip guide',

  'tut.bemvindo.t': 'Welcome to PokeIdle!',
  'tut.bemvindo.b': 'A few quick steps and you will know the essentials: <b>where to hunt</b>, how to <b>heal</b>, what you can <b>automate</b>, and where to <b>sell</b> what you earn. It takes two minutes — and you can skip at any time.',

  'tut.inicial.t': 'Your starter',
  'tut.inicial.b': 'This is your <b>{nome}</b> {tipos}, at level 5. It fights <b>on its own</b>: PokeIdle is an idle game — you choose <i>where</i> to hunt and it does the rest. This panel keeps its HP and XP in sight at all times.',

  'tut.curar.t': 'Heal your team',
  'tut.curar.b': 'You are standing in the <b>Pokémon Center</b> square. When your {nome} faints, this is where you come back to — and <b>Nurse Joy</b> brings the whole team back up <b>for free</b>. Make it a habit: knocked out, click <b>Heal team</b> before heading back to the hunt.',

  'tut.menuMovel.t': 'The Menu button',
  'tut.menuMovel.b': 'On phones, the game screens — Map, Market, Gym, PvP, Shop — live inside the <b>Menu</b> drawer down here. It is the most important button on the bar: whenever this guide mentions a screen, it starts here.',

  'tut.mapa.t': 'The Map',
  'tut.mapa.b': 'The <b>Map</b> is where you pick your hunting ground — and hunting is how both trainer and Pokémon <b>level up</b>. Every area has its own wild species, its own level requirement and its own drops.',

  'tut.hunt.t': 'Pick an easy hunt',
  'tut.hunt.b': 'Your <b>{nome}</b> is a {tipos} type. Tick <b>{tipo}</b> in the type list and turn on <b>“Weak against”</b>: the map then shows only the areas whose wild Pokémon are <b>weak</b> to it. That is the fastest way to kill more and die less early on.',

  'tut.entrarHunt.t': 'Enter the hunt',
  'tut.entrarHunt.b': 'Click an <b>area on the map</b> to start. From there your Pokémon attacks by itself, earns XP and drops wilds without you clicking anything. To switch areas, just come back here.',

  'tut.auto.t': 'Automation',
  'tut.auto.b': 'This panel is the heart of the idle: here you tell the game what to do <b>for you</b> while the hunt runs — use items, throw balls, even head back to the hunt after dying.',

  'tut.itens.t': 'Revive, potion and auto-catch',
  'tut.itens.b': '<b>Use Revive when fainted</b>, <b>Use Potions</b> and <b>Back to the hunt</b> come <b>already on</b>, with your potions and revives already ticked: with them in your bag, your Pokémon heals, gets back up and returns to the hunt on its own — you do not have to touch a thing. <b>Throw until Caught</b> and <b>Throw Nonstop</b> throw Poké Balls for you — those two are a <b>VIP</b> perk.',

  'tut.captura.t': 'Catching by hand',
  'tut.captura.b': 'A defeated wild stays on the ground for a while, in the <b>Close enough to Catch</b> list right here on the stage. Click the <b>Poké Ball</b> next to its name to throw — better ball, better odds. Each species catch rate is in the <b>Pokédex</b>.',

  'tut.market.t': 'Market — buying',
  'tut.market.b': 'The <b>Market</b> is the NPC shop, paid in <b>gold</b>. The <b>Buy</b> tab has Poké Balls, potions, revives and boss arena tickets. Always keep balls and potions in your bag: without them, automation has nothing to work with.',

  'tut.venda.t': 'Selling your drops',
  'tut.venda.b': 'The <b>Sell</b> tab is where everything wild Pokémon drop turns into <b>gold</b>. It is your main income early on: hunt, gather the drops, sell them here and go back with more balls and potions.',

  'tut.vendaPk.t': 'Selling Pokémon',
  'tut.vendaPk.b': 'The <b>Sell Pokémon</b> tab buys the ones you caught and will not use. The price rises with level and rarity — before selling, open the card <b>(i)</b>: if the grade is high, it is worth more on the Community Market.',

  'tut.community.t': 'Community Market (RMT)',
  'tut.community.b': 'This one is <b>player to player</b>: you list what you caught and another trainer buys it. It is where <b>rares and shinies</b> are actually worth something — and where you can get paid straight to your <b>Solana</b> wallet.',

  'tut.resto.t': 'And there is plenty more',
  'tut.resto.b': 'This bar also holds the <b>Gym</b> (18 type gyms, fought over by players), ranked <b>PvP</b> and <b>Guild</b> wars, the <b>Tournament</b>, the 30-day <b>Pass</b>, <b>Bosses</b>, the <b>Pokédex</b>, the <b>Ranking</b>, your <b>House</b>, the <b>Shop</b> and the <b>Poképedia</b> — which documents every calculation the server runs. Explore them at your own pace.',

  'tut.chat.t': 'Still have questions?',
  'tut.chat.b': 'Ask in the <b>chat</b>. There are always people playing, and the community answers fast. Happy hunting, trainer!',

