  'info.casaIntro': 'Gather {n} Key Fragments and this bench crafts a House. The rarity is ROLLED — the rarer it is, the bigger its XP Share slice:',
  'info.colCasa': 'House',
  'info.colBonecos': 'XP Share',
  'info.colChance': 'Chance',
  'info.casaFrag': 'Key Fragments drop in Outland ({chance}% per kill), with no per-account cap. Fragments and finished houses can be traded on the Community Market.',
  'info.casaXpShare': 'Each dummy is a post: register ONE pokémon from your TEAM on it — inside the house or from the House button. While you hunt, it gets the XP share in the table above, of the XP your battling pokémon earns on every kill. Up to {max} houses are in use at the same time, and a pokémon can hold only one post. The registered one gets NOTHING while it is the battling pokémon itself (that one already takes all of it), and the Legendary house registers two.',
  'info.pedraIntro': '{n} Shiny Stone Fragments become ONE stone of the type you choose. The fragment only drops in Outland, at {chance}% per kill — about {media} kills per fragment.',
  'info.pedraAviso': 'If the evolution has no shiny form in the game yet, the evolution is refused — without that, evolving would trade your shiny for a normally coloured pokémon, with no way back. Fragments and finished stones can be traded on the Community Market.',
